From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Kilpatrick <ikilpatrick@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:19:23 -0700
Subject: [gc] Defer CalculationValue handle decrements from ~Length()

`~Length()` may execute during GC sweeping is occurring, and touching
heap objects is disallowed.

Make `CalculationValueHandleMap` queue these decrements into a
non-Oilpan `Vector` to be flushed on subsequent map insert/Increment
operations.

Fixed: 574686297
Change-Id: Ide4aaacc2b58095d6f0b287b20bb3876fae4c172
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8634642
Reviewed-by: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick <ikilpatrick@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1725426}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): this branch has no Length::AssignSlow, so
the conflicting hunks only add DeferredDecrementCalculatedCount() (declaration
and definition) next to DecrementCalculatedCount(); the ~Length() change and
the CalculationValueHandleMap rewrite apply as upstream.

